    "text": "Let G be a group generated by elements x, y, z such that\n\n          x3 = y 2 = z 2 = (xy)3 = (yz)3 = 1    and      g 12 = 1 for all g ∈ G.\n\nIs it true that |G| ⩽ 12?\n    This is true if G is finite (D. V. Lytkina, V. D. Mazurov, Siberian Math. J., 56,\nno. 3 (2015), 471–475).                                                 V. D. Mazurov",
